{"type":"standard","title":"Paul Barringer (attorney)","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Paul Barringer (attorney)</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"titles":{"canonical":"Paul_Barringer_(attorney)","normalized":"Paul Barringer (attorney)","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Paul Barringer (attorney)</span></span>"},"pageid":84635879,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1383732590","tid":"cd194189-d855-11f1-a3a9-896990f28399","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:44:05Z","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Barringer_(attorney)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Barringer_(attorney)?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Barringer_(attorney)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Paul_Barringer_(attorney)"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Barringer_(attorney)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Paul_Barringer_(attorney)","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Barringer_(attorney)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Paul_Barringer_(attorney)"}},"extract":"Paul Barringer is an American attorney and politician from North Carolina. He is the Democratic nominee in the 2026 election for North Carolina's 13th congressional district, running against Brad Knott. He has a bachelor's in environmental history from Davidson College, a Master of Public Administration from the Princeton School of Public and International Affairs, a law degree from the University of North Carolina School of Law and a master's in health policy from Victoria University of Wellington on a Rotary Scholarship.","extract_html":"<p><b>Paul Barringer</b> is an American attorney and politician from North Carolina. He is the Democratic nominee in the 2026 election for North Carolina's 13th congressional district, running against Brad Knott. He has a bachelor's in environmental history from Davidson College, a Master of Public Administration from the Princeton School of Public and International Affairs, a law degree from the University of North Carolina School of Law and a master's in health policy from Victoria University of Wellington on a Rotary Scholarship.</p>"}